(DB-001 - Syrka Supabase MVP Database Architecture) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Status: Implementation Specification) Tj
T*
(Version: 1.0) Tj
T*
(Date: 2026-07-08) Tj
T*
(Builds upon: Product Suite; ADR-001; ADR-002; CEA-001; ONT-001; GRAPH-001; REASON-001; INF-001; ) Tj
T*
(UX-001) Tj
T*
(Decision owners: Database Architecture / Supabase Engineering / Backend Architecture / Security ) Tj
T*
(/ Platform Engineering) Tj
T*
(Scope: Supabase PostgreSQL schemas, tables, RLS, storage buckets, event store, projections, seed) Tj
T*
( data, migrations, implementation order, and future extraction boundaries for Syrka MVP) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(1. Executive Overview) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Supabase PostgreSQL is Syrka's MVP operational backend. It stores the first production-grade ) Tj
T*
(implementation of identity profiles, tenants, institutions, learning projections, canonical ) Tj
T*
(events, ontology terms, evidence, capability observations, recommendations, Odyssey plans, Job ) Tj
T*
(Passport records, employer workflows, faculty dashboards, government aggregates, integration ) Tj
T*
(mappings, storage metadata, and audit logs.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Supabase is the MVP system of record for operational product data, not the permanent replacement) Tj
T*
( for specialized graph, vector, event-store, warehouse, credential-ledger, or object-storage ) Tj
T*
(systems. The schema must therefore be practical enough for Claude Sonnet and backend engineers ) Tj
T*
(to implement quickly while preserving clean extraction paths.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(| Data/system | In Supabase MVP now | Future extraction path |) Tj
T*
(|---|---|---|) Tj
T*
(| Authentication | Supabase Auth + identity schemas | optional enterprise identity broker, still synchronized to ) Tj
T*
(identity projections |) Tj
T*
(| Operational profiles/tenants | PostgreSQL schemas | remains relational source of truth |) Tj
T*
(| Canonical events | PostgreSQL append-only MVP event store | Kafka/NATS + event lake + schema registry |) Tj
T*
(| Ontology | relational tables | RDF/OWL store + graph semantic layer |) Tj
T*
(| Human Capability Graph | relational graph-like projections | Neo4j/property graph + RDF layer |) Tj
T*
(| Evidence metadata | PostgreSQL | stays relational; artifacts in object storage; embeddings in vector DB |) Tj
T*
(| AI embeddings | pgvector optional | dedicated vector database |) Tj
T*
(| Analytics | materialized views/tables | warehouse/lakehouse |) Tj
T*
(| Credential ledger | passport/credential tables | dedicated verifiable credential ledger |) Tj
T*
(| Files/artifacts | Supabase Storage metadata | object storage with scanning/lifecycle policies |) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Avoid overengineering by building only MVP-required tables and projections first, but avoid ) Tj
T*
(lock-in by using canonical IDs, canonical events, source mappings, ontology term IDs, evidence ) Tj
T*
(provenance, RLS, and append-only logs from day one.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(2. Database Architecture Principles) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(1. MVP-first but future-compatible. Build operational tables that support product workflows now ) Tj
T*
(and can be extracted into graph/vector/event systems later.) Tj
T*
(2. Strict tenant isolation. Tenant-scoped rows include tenant_id; RLS policies enforce tenant ) Tj
T*
(access.) Tj
T*
(3. RLS by default. All non-public tables enable Row Level Security before production.) Tj
T*
(4. Canonical IDs. Use Syrka UUIDs/ULIDs as canonical IDs; LMS-native IDs remain mapping fields.) Tj
T*
(5. Event-first architecture. Important state changes publish and/or derive from canonical ) Tj
T*
(events.) Tj
T*
(6. Auditability. Sensitive reads/writes create audit records.) Tj
T*
(7. Evidence provenance. Evidence rows link to canonical events, source systems, artifacts, and ) Tj
ET
